==============================================================================
[B] theorem: the flat-chart single-link marginal is exactly Haar at every beta
==============================================================================
Claim [T].  dmu(U) = prod_l dU_l e^{-S(U)} / Z with S gauge invariant and dU_l the Haar measure.
For any site x let G act as U_{x,mu} -> G U_{x,mu},  U_{x-mu,mu} -> U_{x-mu,mu} G^dag.
That map is a bijection of the configuration space with unit Jacobian and leaves S invariant.
Hence the marginal m(U_l) = int prod_{l'!=l} dU_{l'} e^{-S}/Z satisfies m(G U_l) = m(U_l)
for every G in SU(2); a left-invariant probability density on a compact group is Haar.  [T]
  hypotheses actually used: (i) gauge-invariant action, (ii) product Haar measure,
  (iii) NO gauge-dependent conditioning (no gauge fixing, no center/Polyakov-sector split).

Consequences:
  (B1) (1/3) E|xi_l|^2 = s2 = 3.719824 EXACTLY, for every beta, every L, every dimension.
  (B2) E[chi_flat] = (1/3N) sum_{l,l'} <xi_l.xi_l'> = s2 + Delta,
        Delta = (1/3N) sum_{l != l'} <xi_l.xi_l'>   (the ONLY beta-dependent piece)
  (B3) beta=0: links iid => Delta = 0 => chi_flat = 3.719824 exactly, all L (corpus D6/D1/P5).
  (B4) the same identity holds for 2D, 3D, any N, any lattice geometry: chi_flat is dimension-free.
  (B5) the plaquette is NOT constrained by (B1): it is a 4-link correlated object and can move
       5.29x while the 1-link marginal is exactly constant.  => all beta-dependence lives in Delta.

