==============================================================================
[E] dilution: what the L-scan can still say about a box-gap family on THIS carrier
==============================================================================
The family of GY3 1.1 (single box-gap atom, residue f1^2) contributes X(L) = f1^2/(4 sin^2(pi/L)),
i.e. chi_flat(L) = s2 + f1^2 * chi_box(L).  Subtraction of s2 is exact [T], so the honest test is
absolute, not a ratio of totals.
  L  chi_box  pred f=1     meas     se     dev  sigma f1^2 2sig ub
  4   0.5000    4.2198   3.7654 0.0498  0.4544    9.1       0.2904
  6   1.0000    4.7198   3.7581 0.0624  0.9617   15.4       0.1631
  8   1.7071    5.4269   3.8218 0.0633  1.6051   25.4       0.1339
 12   3.7321    7.4519   3.6589 0.1903  3.7930   19.9       0.0857
 16   6.5685   10.2884   3.7055 0.1759  6.5829   37.4       0.0514
  (the corpus GY3-NOGAP-NUM.md:131 quotes 111 sigma from 3.414 vs 1.015+-0.022: that compares
   ratios of TOTALS, where the additive s2 dilutes the family ratio 3.414 -> 1.286.  The honest
   absolute test is stronger and lands at 9-37 sigma, with the binding bound f1^2 <= 0.051 at L=16.)
  GY3 merged beta=2.5: chi(4) = 3.7654+-0.0498, chi(8) = 3.8218+-0.0633, ratio = 1.0150+-0.0212
  ratio test with the family f1^2=1: pred 5.4269/4.2198 = 1.2861 -> 12.8 sigma
  => the L-scan survives as a carrier-specific bound: a box-gap atom on the flat-chart log field
     with f1^2 >= 0.051 (2 sigma, L=16) is excluded; below that it is invisible.

==============================================================================
[F] acid tests
==============================================================================
  F1  beta=0 pure Haar: chi_flat = s2 exactly, every L.  corpus D6-DECISION:135 prints
      Var(a) = 3.7198 for L=1..8 (L-independent) [T].  PASSES -- and this is the tell:
      the same number is returned at beta=2.5, i.e. the estimator cannot tell beta=0 from beta=2.5.
  F2  free massive scalar (m=1): Var(a) = 1/m^2 = 1.000, L-independent (D1 exact);
      free massless scalar: Var = 1/(4 sin^2(pi/L)) = 0.500 / 1.707 / 3.732 / 6.569 (L=4/8/12/16)
      -> grows like L^2/(4pi^2).  So the *scalar* estimator is fine; it is the GAUGE-ORBIT
      marginal (B1) that the acid tests never exercised: D1/M1 acid tests use scalars, no gauge
      symmetry, no Haar orbit => they cannot see the failure mode.
  F3  2D YM: (B1)-(B4) are dimension-free, so chi_flat(2D) = 3.7198 + Delta_2D as well.
      A channel that returns the same number for the solvable/gapped 2D theory and for 4D at
      every beta cannot separate them.  Per CLAUDE.md 1.1 (a tool must fail on the acid case),
      chi_flat is acid-vacuous *as a beta/L discriminator for gauge theories*.
  F4  chart acid (already measured, M1-4D-RUN.md:38): the SAME beta=2.5 ensemble gives
      chi_Landau = 36.98 / 58.61 / 115.30 (L=4/6/8) vs chi_flat 3.81/3.76/3.82.
      Chart changes the number by 10-30x at FIXED beta; beta changes it by 3%.
      => the leading term of the reading is the gauge orbit, by two orders of magnitude.

