  <1/2 Re tr U_l> = 0  and  sd = 1/sqrt(8) = 0.3536  (Haar),  at EVERY beta, while the plaquette
  (a 4-link joint object) moves freely.
  exact SU(3) Haar (torus quadrature): <1/2 Re tr U> = -6.74e-18, sd = 0.3536, frac(|s|>0.9) = 0.014, min = -0.750
  beta=2.2   links= 1024  <1/2 Re tr U> = -0.02005 +- 0.0110  sd = 0.3532  frac(|s|>0.9) = 0.017  min = -0.687  plaq = 0.8595
